- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sopinvoke.html
- Summary (EN): SOP Invoke runs a compiled SOP block on its inputs. It converts incoming COP layers into geometry and passes that geometry to the block's matching inputs.
- Résumé (FR) : SOP Invoke exécute un bloc SOP compilé sur des entrées COP converties en géométrie, qu'il reçoit sur ses entrées correspondantes.

- Inputs meaning: ["input1, input2, ...: each receives COP data converted to geometry for the matching input of the compiled SOP block; the count is set by the Inputs parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Inputs: number of inputs", "Input #: name (not a path) of the Input Name on the Block Begin Compile SOP inside the subnetwork that this input overrides", "Outputs: number of outputs", "Output Node #: path to the Block End Compile SOP of the block to run", "Unload Behavior: Never (cache), Use Node's Flag, or Always (no cache, default, less memory)"]

- Caveats: ["Node parameters inside the invoked block are evaluated in their original locations, not through this node's interface", "Distinct from the Invoke Block node listed in the same category"]

